WEBVTT

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:29.920
January 1953, the eyes of the world were on the White House.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.090
in Washington, D.C., where Harry S. Truman greeted his successor, Dwight D. Eisenhower,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:40.200
new president of the United States. After 20 years, a Republican returned to the White

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.120
House. Ike, as he is familiarly known to fellow Americans, receiving his oath from the Chief

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:53.850
Justice, the late Fred M. Vinson. A dramatic moment in the life of a soldier statesman,

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:59.510
now the 35th president of the United States. Dwight D. Eisenhower and his vice president,

00:00:59.650 --> 00:00:59.970
Richard D.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.870
Nixon. The names of two lawmakers, Taft and Hartley, were prominent in the news, and the death

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:13.440
of Senator Robert Taft, Mr. Republican, co-author of the controversial labor bill, saddened the

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.560
nation. Bob Taft had earned the respect of friend and foe alike. The president lost a wise guide

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:28.040
and counselor. The death of Russia's premier Joseph Stalin was big news in 1953. Of two

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.960
Stalinaires, Malenkov, one out of

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.420
and the free world wondered what next from the Kremlin.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.480
Good news for the free world from West Germany, where Chancellor Atenauer won re-election,

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:46.080
pledging Germany's continued support of NATO and the West, a resounding no to communism.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:53.780
Vatican City, Rome, Pope Pius XII presiding over the consistory,

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:59.360
elevating new members to the College of Cardinals, scenes of ancient religious pomp and ceremony.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:05.230
The Cardinals designate prostrating themselves before the altar to take the vows of high office.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.090
James Cardinal McIntyre of Los Angeles was one of the new princes of the church.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:21.520
Canada's first general election in four years brought five and one-half million eligible voters to the polls.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.260
Victory went to the liberal incumbents led by Prime Minister Saint Laurent.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.980
Coronation Fleet Review at Spithead for England's new...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.220
Queen Elizabeth II, the greatest peacetime fleet in history, in a salute to Britain's newly crowned

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:40.560
monarch. Even Russian ships were there. Diplomatic courtesy to the new Elizabeth, Britain's hoped

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:55.000
would bring back the glory of ancient Elizabethan time. 53, year of disasters brought into sharp

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.970
focus in Holland. The worst storms in 500 years lashed the North Sea. Blood time.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.840
and hurricane winds pounded the dikes. For centuries, Holland's bulwark against the sea.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.380
Despite heroic efforts to reinforce the dikes, the sea broke through, inundating one-sixth of the

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:15.520
country. Land rested from the sea centuries ago was lost to the raging torrent temporarily.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.000
During the nightmare of flood and terror, thousands lost their lives. But Holland faced

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:29.970
disaster bravely, with help and sympathy from a queen. Disaster struck

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.100
in Greece, too. Earthquakes jarred the fabled Ionian Isle. For days, the earth shook. Buildings,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:42.020
then entire towns toppled. Trapped in the ruins, hundreds perished and thousands were injured.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:46.730
U.S. Navy units assisted in the rescue and relief of the stunned islanders,

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.260
who buried their dead and faced the cruel task of reconstruction.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.140
Disaster left scars that will take a long time to heal.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.480
The June Rebellion of enslaved workers in East Berlin and elsewhere behind the Iron Curtain

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.220
gave tangible proof to free men that all was not well with communism.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.460
Rioting Berliners turned on their commie masters,

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.170
batting their pat-up spleen on red officials,

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.720
and police were powerless to stop them.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.500
For days, anti-reds rioted in East Berlin,

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.960
and only the arrival of Russia...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.080
tanks and troops saved the day

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.040
for Moscow-trained stooges in power

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.080
in East Germany. The temper of the

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.040
enslaved peoples was graphically displayed.

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.770
Men threw rocks at tanks.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.240
All was not well behind the Iron Curtain.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.660
In contrast to violence in East Berlin

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.780
were scenes like these in West Berlin

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.500
where East Berliners lined up

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.780
quietly to receive food, much of it

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.960
a gift of the United States.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.950
A weapon in the Cold War, freedom's answer to hunger riots behind the Iron Curtain.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.480
Freedom bomb posed the problems of preventing war and protecting citizens.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.610
Real houses with unreal occupants placed in the target area during tests

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:24.540
could help men answer the question, is there any defense against the bomb?

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.240
Fury of the unleashed atom strikes the house.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.510
The first atomic cannon.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:54.590
An atomic punch on the ground as well as in the air gave us a powerful new weapon of defense.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.660
Another deterrent against aggression.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.980
Six of the new guns were shipped to Europe during the year to...

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:12.620
forces of freedom in the defense against communist imperialism a kangaroo with wing the 36 bomber

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:18.150
converted into a flying aircraft carrier long-range bombers could fly close to enemy targets

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:24.080
at least the atom bomb carrying jet fighters to dive down to the attack range of the bomber plus

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:29.720
speed of the fighter effectively combined for swift retaliation in case of enemy attack on these

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.180
States. Mission completed, jet returns to Mother Plane, catching the hook suspended from the bomb

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:53.960
bay. New weapons and new methods to keep us strong and free. Korea, top story of 1953, the end of

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:59.070
three years of bitter, costly conflict. The agreement was signed for the United Nations by

00:06:59.070 --> 00:06:59.910
General William Harris.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.680
for the Reds by North Korea's Nam-i-yoo.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.870
Big problems remained to be solved at the conference table,

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.240
but a big step forward had been taken,

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.090
and the last shell was fired on the Korean front,

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.750
at least for the time being.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.390
What lay ahead no man could prophesy,

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:18.370
but for these G.I.s at least the war was over.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.690
They were alive and going home.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:28.440
At Freedom Gate came the POW,

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:29.970
prisoners of the Reds.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.710
Reds for long months and years, many of them sick in body and mind, but they smiled now

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:43.620
that freedom was here. Others were not so fortunate. Torture, neglect, death at the

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:50.300
hands of the communists. Free men would not forget. General William Dean, the hero of

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:55.180
Tayshon, back from three years of captivity. Arrogant to the last were the prisoners we

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:59.850
released. In a defiant gesture, the die-hard Reds discarded their clothing, providing

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.040
by the UNLI.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.330
A grim lesson to the free world.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:08.070
that the truce in Korea might well be but the prelude to aggression elsewhere in the world.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.780
1953 brought hopes for peace.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:14.490
But in a world split by isms and by fears,

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:18.670
Americans pondered the lessons of Korea and gave heed to their president.

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:26.080
We have won an armistice on a single battleground.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:27.540
Not.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.050
Peace in the world.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:34.340
we may not now relax our guard nor cease our quest.
